{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"P2 SCOPE EXTENSION (review-driven): Gerrit change 2035 patchset 2 drew a blocking LLM-Review finding — the widened T13 lexicon was partly UNREACHABLE because the unchanged deterministic pre-gate regex (det_gate_rules.py, mechanism-of-enforcement) does not match several additive-only phrasings ('callers must', 'every X must', 'must stay in sync/in step', 'new contract/invariant/schema field', 'adds a required …'), so such plans would be det-skipped before the router. Fix in patchset 3: a second alternation branch with the additive-obligation lexicon is appended to the T13 pre-gate; the audit-verbatim enforcement branch (ticket 696a) stays byte-for-byte; fires-side unit coverage added (5 new sentences in test_det_criterion_gates.py); routing trigger text updated to state the pre-gate covers both vocabularies. This supersedes the earlier note that the det gate was untouched — the description's Approach/Scope and the ticket file_impact now record the two extra files. Patchset 1 also failed CI on the prompt front-matter canonical-form test (frontmatter must round-trip through write_front_matter); fixed by canonicalizing the edited frontmatter in patchset 2."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787356218498524001,"uuid":"c7c874ed-cf95-48e5-beed-e2d93a08cdc4"}